The native adaptation constructs saturated ideal predicates over checked
commutative setoid rings. Finite expression witnesses define spans; explicit
coefficient/member witnesses define principal ideals and sums. Products are
actual spans of products. Universal properties and ring laws prove the ideal
operations, without importing the full Submodule/typeclass hierarchy.

Coordinate point classes and X/Y/XY ideals adapt the pinned
Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Affine/Point.lean, whose existing
attribution is retained in NOTICE.FLT. The initial pair-product expansion
is proved. The point-evaluation quotient, nonsingular inverse/addition
identities, class group, injection and full point group laws remain open.
